# Root .dockerignore.
#
# This file is used only by the Dockerfile.web build, and only because that
# build's context has to be the repository root: the Caddyfile lives at the
# root and has to be copied into the image, while the SPA is built from
# apps/web. Dockerfile.api's context is apps/api, so this does not affect it.
#
# The context is narrowed to just those two things rather than shipped whole —
# apps/api alone is a few MB of source that the SPA image does not contain.

*
!Caddyfile
!apps/web

# And inside apps/web, only what `npm run build` reads.
apps/web/node_modules
apps/web/dist
apps/web/e2e
apps/web/playwright.config.ts

# The generated api client is deliberately NOT excluded from the build by being
# copied in: it is git-ignored and is regenerated in the image from the
# committed openapi.json. Excluding it here is what stops a developer's stale
# src/generated from silently becoming the deployed bundle.
apps/web/src/generated

**/.DS_Store
**/*.log